 RC HANDLING (DB.1 COND-CODE TESTS)
   ALL JOBS : RC 0 AND 4 = NORMAL COMPLETION
              RC 4 FROM PSEOD01, CUSTMNT2, CRDMNT1, PYINB01 RAISES AN
              INFORMATIONAL TICKET (SERVICE NOW ASSIGNMENT GROUP IN
              THE JOB HEADER) - NETWORK CONTINUES
              RC > 4 OR ABEND = NETWORK HELD, ON-CALL PAGED
   INACR01  : RC 4 = ACCOUNTS WITH NO PRODUCT PARAMETERS - TICKET TO
              CORE SYSTEMS - DDA, NETWORK CONTINUES
   GLFEED01 : RC 8 FROM GL030 = FEED NOT SENT. NETWORK HELD - CALL
              FINANCE SYSTEMS BEFORE RELEASING MBKDTROL (THE FEED
              MUST GO WITH TODAY'S BUSINESS DATE)
   INCAP01  : NOT RERUNNABLE AFTER COMMIT - ON ABEND CALL DDA ON-CALL
              (DBA DELETES MBK.INTPAID ROWS FOR THE RUN FIRST)
   FXRAT01  : RC 8 = FIXING FILE REJECTED, OLD RATES STAY IN FORCE.
              NOT IN A NETWORK - CALL TREASURY OPERATIONS
   ODREV01  : RC 4 = EXCEPTIONS ON THE REPORT, NETWORK CONTINUES.
              U1005 = DATE CARD GAP CHECK FAILED - DO NOT RESTART
              UNTIL THE DATE CARD HAS BEEN CHECKED (INC 16/0042).
              RERUN ONLY AFTER RESTORING ACCTMAST (SEE JOB HEADER)
   CSSDLY01 : RC > 4 OR ABEND - PAGE PAYMENTS IT (ROTA PAY) AT ONCE,
              CASSOUT MUST REACH BACSTEL-IP BY 02:00
   BCPEXT01 : BCP CRITICAL. FIX AND RERUN BEFORE 06:30 OR THE BRANCHES
              OPEN WITH YESTERDAY'S FILE - INFORM THE IT SERVICE
              CONTINUITY DUTY MANAGER. RC 4 = EXCEPTIONS, CONTINUE.
              U1004 = TOO FEW ACCOUNTS (CHECK THE ACCTMAST RESTORE)
   MIEXT01  : U1004 = DIMENSION TOTALS DISAGREE - CALL CORE SYSTEMS
   CHGTAR01 : RC 4 = REPORT TO CHARGING OPERATIONS. BEFORE A RERUN
              DELETE THE BAD MBK.PRD.CHG.ANNSUMM GENERATION
   PSARC01  : RC 4 = MAXROWS REACHED OR ROWS ALREADY DELETED. ON
              ABEND RESUBMIT UNCHANGED (RESTARTS FROM THE CHECKPOINT
              MBK.PRD.TXNHIST.CHKPT). DBA THEN RUNS MBKREOTX
   RGBOE01  : RC 4 = EXCEPTIONS OR LATE RUN - REGULATORY REPORTING
              REVIEW THE REPORT BEFORE SUBMISSION
   SVSWP01  : RC 4 = SWEEPS FAILED (REPORT SWP1) - SAVINGS OPERATIONS
              NEXT MORNING, NETWORK CONTINUES. ON ABEND RERUN FROM
              SW004 - DO NOT RESTORE ACCTMAST (DONE SWEEPS ARE SKIPPED)
   CMPRD01  : RC 4 = ITEMS REJECTED BACK TO CMS - NO OPS ACTION.
              U1004/U1006/U1007 = BAD INPUT FILE, NOTHING WAS PAID -
              ASK CMS SUPPORT TO RESEND, THEN RERUN
   ATMSTL01 : RC 4 = EXCEPTIONS - REPORT TO CARD SERVICES. U1004 =
              LINK TRAILER OR NET SETTLEMENT DISAGREES - DO NOT RERUN,
              CALL PAYMENTS OPERATIONS (LINK SETTLEMENT DESK)
   PYBGC01  : RC 4 = SLIP DIFFERENCES / SUSPENSE ITEMS FOR BRANCHES.
              U1004 = IMAGE FILE INCOMPLETE - DO NOT RERUN UNTIL
              BRANCH OPERATIONS RESEND IT
   DDALR01  : RC 4 = ALERTS NOT SENT (NO MOBILE OR EMAIL) - REPORT
              ALR1 TO THE CONTACT CENTRE. AL020 STILL RUNS
   IBFEED03 : RC 4 = CONTROL EXCEPTIONS (REPORT IB31), FEED IS SENT -
              TICKET TO DDA OPERATIONS. U1004 = TXNHIST CHANGED -
              CHECK PSEOD01 HAS ENDED, THEN RERUN
   SARXT01  : RC 4 = REQUEST REJECTED OR OVERDUE - THE DPO MUST ACT
              TODAY. SAROUT IS CLASS P (PERSONAL DATA) - DO NOT
              RE-ROUTE IT
   TAXCR01  : RC 4 = CHASE ENTRIES WRITTEN (NORMAL)

 NOTES
   1. CFDEC01 IS SUBMITTED AT 19:00 (THE BEREAVEMENT TEAM'S CUT-OFF)
      BUT OPENS CIFMAST, ACCTMAST, SOMAST, DDMAND AND LOANMAST WITH
      DISP=OLD. IT IS HELD ON MBKONLDN SO IT DOES NOT HANG ON THE
      ENQUEUE WHILE CICS HAS THE FILES OPEN. DECPOST STILL REACHES
      TONIGHT'S PSEOD01 (PSEOD01 REQUIRES CFDEC01).
   2. MBKONLDN CLOSES (AND MBKONLUP REOPENS) 20 CICS FILES: ACCTMST,
      CIFMAST, MEMOLOG, PSTXREF, SOMAST, DDMAND, DDHOLD, CHGPEND,
      PRDPARM, LOANMST, LOANCIF, ACCTNOC, CIFCTL, SAVNTC (INNTC01),
      CHQSTOP, STMTADH (STMT01 ST012/ST016), SWITCHES (CSSDLY01),
      SAVSWP (SVSWP01), ALRTPRF (DDALR01) AND TAXCERT (TAXCR01).
      ANY JOB THAT UPDATES
      ONE OF THESE FILES MUST REQUIRE MBKONLDN. FXRATES STAYS OPEN -
      FXRAT01 RUNS IN THE ONLINE DAY.
   3. CFKYC01 UPDATES CIFMAST (DISP=OLD) ON SUNDAY MORNING WHEN CICS
      HAS IT OPEN. OPERATIONS CLOSE CIFMAST (CEMT) AND RELEASE THE
      JOB, THEN REOPEN CIFMAST WHEN IT ENDS.
   4. (IF SCHED) = REQUIREMENT ONLY WHEN THE PREDECESSOR IS SCHEDULED
      THAT DAY (DEMAND, EVENT-TRIGGERED OR MONTHLY JOBS).
   5. ALL JOBS IN MBKEOD READ THE DATE CARD (PROCS MBKBATCH/MBKDB2B)
      AND MUST END BEFORE MBKDTROL ROLLS THE BUSINESS DATE.
      ODAUSWP1 AND CPAUSWP1 (IDCAMS/MBKOPCMD ONLY) DO NOT READ IT.
   6. CFMRG01 UPDATES CIFMAST, ACCTMAST AND LOANMAST (DISP=OLD) AT
      20:00 SATURDAY WHILE CICS HAS THEM OPEN. AS FOR CFKYC01,
      OPERATIONS CLOSE ACCTMST, CIFMAST AND LOANMST (CEMT), RELEASE
      THE JOB AND REOPEN THE FILES WHEN IT ENDS. IT MUST END BEFORE
      MBKONLDN (23:30) SO THAT TONIGHT'S MBKEOD IS NOT DELAYED.
   7. CHLGSWP1, ODAUSWP1, CPAUSWP1 SWEEP THE CICS EXTRA-PARTITION
      AUDIT QUEUES (CHLG IN MBKCORE, ODAU/CPAU IN MBKCOR3). AT 00:30
      OPERATIONS AUTOMATION SWITCHES CHLG TO ITS ALTERNATE DATASET
      (MBK.PRD.CICS.CHLG.ALT) AND CLOSES ODAU/CPAU. ODAUSWP1/CPAUSWP1
      CLOSE AND REOPEN THEIR QUEUE THEMSELVES (SW005/SW020). THEY ARE
      TIME-SCHEDULED AND INDEPENDENT OF MBKONLDN.
   8. CSSDLY01 IS TRIGGERED BY THE CASS INBOUND FILE. CS010/CS020
      UPDATE ACCTMAST, SOMAST, DDMAND AND THE CICS FILE SWITCHES, SO
      IT ALSO REQUIRES MBKONLDN. ITS CSSPOST FEED AND INNTC01'S
      NTCPOST FEED ARE HARD POSTED BY TONIGHT'S PSEOD01, WHICH WAITS
      FOR BOTH (CSSDLY01 ONLY IF THE FILE HAS ARRIVED).
   9. BCPEXT01 TAKES THE FINAL ACCOUNT POSITION FOR THE BRANCH
      CONTINGENCY PCS AND THE DR SITE, SO IT WAITS FOR EVERY OTHER
      JOB IN THE NIGHT'S RUN AND MBKDTROL WAITS FOR BCPEXT01 ONLY.
      IF BCPEXT01 IS FORCE-COMPLETED, CHECK THAT ALL ITS REQUIREMENTS
      HAVE ENDED BEFORE MBKDTROL IS RELEASED.
  10. RGBOE01 READS THE BALANCES AS AT QUARTER END, SO IT MUST END
      BEFORE THE FIRST PSEOD01 OF THE NEW QUARTER POSTS. PSEOD01
      WAITS FOR IT ON THE DAYS IT IS SCHEDULED.
  11. SVSWP01 SWEEPS ON THE PROJECTED BALANCE - AVAILABLE BALANCE LESS
      THE DEBITS ALREADY QUEUED IN SOPOST, DDPOST, CHQPOST, CRDPOST
      AND LNREPAY. IT WAITS FOR CQCLR01 AND CDSTL01 WHEN THEY ARE
      SCHEDULED SO TONIGHT'S CHEQUE AND CARD DEBITS ARE COUNTED. ITS
      SWPPOST FEED IS HARD POSTED BY TONIGHT'S PSEOD01.
  12. PYBGC01, ATMSTL01 AND CMPRD01 ARE EVENT-TRIGGERED AFTER
      MBKONLDN. THEIR FEEDS (BGCPOST, ATMPOST, RDRPOST) ARE HARD
      POSTED BY TONIGHT'S PSEOD01, WHICH WAITS FOR THEM WHEN THEIR
      FILE HAS ARRIVED. THEIR GL JOURNALS (BGCS, ATMS, CMPL) GO TO
      GLFEED01 STEP GL020. PYBGC01 ALSO RUNS BEFORE CQCLR01 - BOTH
      UPDATE THE UNCLEARED CHEQUES FILE MBK.PRD.CHQ.UNCLEARED.
  13. DDALR01 UPDATES ALRTPRF, SO IT MUST END BEFORE MBKONLUP REOPENS
      THE FILE - BCPEXT01 WAITS FOR IT. THE ALERT GATEWAY HOLDS THE
      MESSAGES UNTIL 07:00 (NO SMS OVERNIGHT - FCA GUIDANCE).

